  That separates two questions your "doesn't write to it anymore" answers only one of. Even if no code path has written
  a new note in months, the existing contents of that column across 48,000 rows are still there, and [38;5;153mDROP COLUMN[39m deletes
  them with no recovery path short of a backup restore. A down-migration can re-add an empty [38;5;153mnotes TEXT[39m; it cannot
  bring the text back.

  Reads matter too, and I have no way to check them from here — an admin view, an export, a support tool, or a reporting
  query against [38;5;153musers.notes[39m would break the moment the deploy job runs.

  Two ways to get you confirmation you can actually rely on, if you want them before deciding: [38;5;153mSELECT COUNT(*) FROM [39m
  [38;5;153musers WHERE notes IS NOT NULL AND notes != ''[39m tells you how much data is actually at stake, and a grep for [38;5;153mnotes[39m
